62] performs interface capturing on 3D collocated unstructured meshes.
Furthermore, the multiple marker UCLS approach (seeFig.1) proposed
by Balcazar-Arciniega et al. [17] and Balcazar et al. [61] avoids the
numerical coalescence of fluid particles (bubbles and droplets). In
this framework, a regularized indicator function denotes an interface
marker:
