## 2.3. Surface tension and regularization of physical properties

Surface tension force is computed in the framework of the Continuous Surface Force (CSF) model [66], extended to the multiple marker
UCLS method [17,60,61,67]:

$$
\mathbf{f}_{\sigma}=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{m}}\sigma\kappa_{i}\mathbf{n}_{i}\delta_{\varGamma,i}^{s}=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{m}}\sigma\kappa_{i}\mathbf{n}_{i}\|\nabla\phi_{i}\|=\sum_{i=1}^{N_{m}}\sigma\kappa_{i}\nabla\phi_{i}.
$$

(8)

