## 4.1.1. Grid convergence

$$
A_{i}(t)=\int_{\Omega}\delta_{\Gamma,i}^{s}d V,\delta_{\Gamma,i}^{s}=\|\nabla\phi_{i}\|[29,65]
$$

*𝛺* is a cylinder with height *𝐻𝛺* and diameter *𝐷𝛺*. Triangular prism
control volumes discretize *𝛺*, as depicted inFig.3b. Due to the trajectory instability of bubbles as the Reynolds number increases, interactions between bubbles and the cylinder wall become significant. To
capture the bouncing effect on bubbles near the wall as depicted in
Fig.4andFig.5, the mesh has been refined in this region. Meshes
have been generated by a constant step extrusion of a two-dimensional
unstructured grid along the *𝑦*-axis, being the step size *𝐻𝛺*∕*𝑁*<sub>𝑝</sub>= *ℎ*<sub>𝑚𝑎𝑥</sub>,
*𝑁*<sub>𝑝</sub>denotes the number of planes in which the *𝑦*-axis is divided. Close
to the wall, *ℎ*<sub>𝑚𝑖𝑛</sub>∼ *ℎ*<sub>𝑚𝑎𝑥</sub>∕3 where *ℎ*<sub>𝑚𝑎𝑥</sub>is the grid size around the centre
of the pipe, as outlined inTable1.

$$
D_{\varOmega}.
$$

$$
H_{\varOmega}/N_{p}=h_{m a x},
$$

