$$

The cylinder wall is subjected to a no-slip boundary condition
for velocity, while a Neumann boundary condition is applied for the
concentration of chemical species. Dirichlet condition is set for UCLS
markers on the wall, i.e., *𝜙*<sub>𝑖</sub>= 0 if *𝜙*<sub>𝑖</sub>*<* 0*.*5 defines *𝛺*<sub>𝑑</sub>, or *𝜙*<sub>𝑖</sub>= 1
