## 4.4. Drag force and mass transfer in bubble swarms in a vertical pipe

$$
\mathrm{C_D}
$$

Once single bubbles in a vertical pipe have been researched, Direct
Numerical Simulations (DNS) are conducted for drag force and reactive
mass transfer in a swarm of bubbles rising in a full periodic cube
and periodic pipe at Re = *𝑂*(100 − 1000). The multi-marker UCLS
approach [17,59] is employed to prevent the numerical coalescence of
bubbles [59]. The Reynolds number is calculated according toEqs.(27)
and(28). Following the work of Simonnet et al. [107], Roghair et al.
[15] and Gillissen et al. [108], when bubbles move in a swarm the
magnitude of the buoyancy force is lower as compared with a single
bubble, because of the effect of the mixture density. Therefore, the
balance between gravity and drag forces has to account for this effect.
Consequently, CD in bubble swarms is calculated as follows:

(45)

$$
\frac{\mathrm{C}_{\mathrm{D}}}{1-\alpha}=\frac{4}{3}\frac{d_{b}\left(\rho_{c}-\rho_{d}\right)g}{\rho_{c}\mathrm{U_{r}}^{2}},
$$

$$
\mathrm{Re}=O(100-1000)
$$

where the corrective term (1− *𝛼*) is added in the drag formulation as
compared to the isolated bubble case (Eq.(33)).

For simulations in a periodic pipe (Fig.23), *𝛺* is discretized by
the mesh *𝑀*<sub>9</sub>as detailed inTable1, with grid size {*ℎ*<sub>𝑚𝑎𝑥</sub>*, ℎ*<sub>𝑚𝑖𝑛</sub>} =
{*𝑑*<sub>𝑏</sub>∕40*, ℎ*<sub>𝑚𝑎𝑥</sub>∕3} (seeFig.3). For a full periodic cube (Fig.24), *𝛺* is
discretized by the mesh *𝑀*<sub>5</sub>(Table5), comprising hexahedral control
volumes with a uniform grid size of *ℎ* = *𝑑*<sub>𝑏</sub>∕40*.*65. Boundary conditions
for the periodic pipe remain consistent with those used for bubbles in
a pipe, as discussed in Section4.1.1. However, in the cube scenario, all
boundaries are configured as periodic. The initial conditions involve a
random distribution of *𝑁*<sub>𝑏</sub>bubbles in *𝛺*, whereas the fluid is quiescent.
Since bubble coalescence is avoided [17,59] and the flow is incompressible, {*𝑁*<sub>𝑏</sub>*,𝛼*} are kept constant throughout simulations. Dimensionless
parameters are Eo = 3*.*125, Mo = 10<sup>−11</sup>, *𝜂* = 100, *𝜂* = 100, Sc = 1,
