In addition,Fig.26depicts a parity plot {Cc*,* Cc,FM}, where Cc
denotes DNS predictions, and Cc,FMrefers to results calculated with the
film model as reported by Roghair et al. [16]. This theory assumes a
stagnant film layer around the interface at a local steady-state, where
diffusion and chemical reaction influence the mass transfer of chemical
species. On the other hand, chemical species outside this film layer
are assumed to be perfectly mixed by the turbulence. In the range of
dimensionless numbers used in this research, DNS predictions are in
close agreement with the film theory, as depicted inFig.26for both
the periodic vertical pipe and the fully periodic cube.

