On the other hand, DNS of bubble swarms in a periodic vertical
pipe and fully periodic cube have been performed in the framework of
the multi-marker UCLS method [17]. DNS predictions of CD in a fully
periodic cube are consistent with the correlation proposed by Roghair
et al. [16]. Concerning the interfacial area of bubbles in a swarm, A<sup>∗</sup>
decreases with *𝛼*. As *𝛼* tends to zero A<sup>∗</sup>is closer to results predicted by
Eq.(43), as well as correlations of Liu et al. [95] and Besagni and Deen
[97]. Concerning the mass transfer in bubbles in a swarm, ShPe<sup>−1∕2</sup>
increases with *𝛼*, whereas the film-theory leads to accurate predictions
for C<sub>c</sub>, within the range of conditions explored in this research.

