## Appendix A. Interface deformation

The ability of UCLS method to capture extreme interface deformations is proven with the 3D deformation field proposed by LeVeque
[79] and Enright et al. [111]. A sphere of *𝑑*<sub>𝑏</sub>= 0*.*3 is centred at
(0*.*35, 0*.*35, 0*.*35). *𝛺* is a cubic domain of unit side length (Fig.3a).
The convective term of the interface transport equation (Eq.(18)) is
solved with unstructured flux-limiters, whereas two steps (*𝛥𝜏*) of the reinitialization equation (Eq.(19)) are applied. Momentum transport and
mass transfer equation solvers are disconnected, whereas an external
velocity field is applied:
