*𝛼* = 1 leads to the minimum interface thickness, whereas the tiny
lamella structure is captured at *𝑡* = 0*.*5*𝑇*. If *𝛼* = 0*.*9, the interface
thickness increases. Furthermore, the interface breaks at *𝑡* = 0*.*5*𝑇*.
Fig.28c shows the effect of the flux-limiter (SUPERBEE, MINMOD,
SMART, UPWIND), setting *𝛼* = 1. The predicted sphericity at *𝑡* = *𝑇*
using MINMOD and UPWIND limiters depart from results using SMART
and SUPERBEE limiters due to the numerical diffusion. Results with
SMART and SUPERBEE limiter better approximate the initial droplet
sphericity (*𝛹* = 1).

